 "result_text": "Equation fields now use Knack's own formatted value for `.formatted`, so the days-vs-seconds case from the issue should come out as 4 instead of 372171.318. I haven't run anything, including the test suite, so this is untested.\n\nThe change is one line in `knackpy/models.py`: I added `\"equation\": {\"use_knack_format\": True}` to `FIELD_SETTINGS`. That's the same mechanism `timer` and `name` already use. `.raw` still holds the `field_377_raw` value.\n\nOne edge case: if Knack's formatted value is falsy, such as `0` or an empty string, `Field._format` in `knackpy/fields.py` falls back to the raw value. So a formatted `0` could still show the raw number. I left that check alone because it applies to every field type.",
